<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine garment exports down 2.82 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Philippine garment exports down 2.82 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Export receipts from Philippine garments and textile slipped by 2.82 percent to $2.787 billion in 1996 from $2.868 billion in the previous year, documents released by the Garments &amp; Textile Export Board (GTEB) on Tuesday said.</p>
<p>Exports to quota countries went down to $2.107 billion from $2.245 billion. Quota countries include the United States, European Union and Canada which have committed to buy a certain volume of textile products from the Philippines each year.</p>
<p>Exports to the United States, the country's biggest buyer, went down to $1.649 billion from $1.771 billion in the previous year. - Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
</text>
